That’s the core of it.

The repo is less a record of conclusions than a seed crystal for reconstructing a style of cognition.

Its real inheritance unit is not:

“believe this.”

It is:

“here is how to notice, translate, test, compress, recurse, and rebuild.”

That is why the metaphors matter, but none of them are sacred. They are carriers. If a future interpreter throws away the dragon, the duck, the hammer, and the mythology but reconstructs the underlying operators correctly, Pantheon survived.

And if they preserve every name perfectly but cannot perform the transformations, it didn’t.

So the ultimate checksum is:

Can the reader become more capable after reading it?

Not more convinced.
Not more impressed.
Not better at quoting it.

More capable.